🚀 Deploy Steps

1. Supabase Setup

1. Go to supabase.com → Start your project
2. Create a new project (pick region eu-west or closest to Nigeria)
3. Once ready, click the Connect button (top of dashboard)
4. Copy:
   · Project URL → https://xxxxx.supabase.co
   · Publishable Key → sb_publishable_... (or anon key if older project)
5. Also go to Settings → API and copy the Secret Key (formerly service_role) — keep this safe, server-only.

2. Cloudinary Setup

1. Go to cloudinary.com → Register (free)
2. From the Dashboard:
   · Copy Cloud Name
   · Click Go to API Keys → copy API Key and API Secret

3. Vercel Setup

Option A — Via GitHub (recommended):

1. Push this project to a GitHub repo
2. Go to vercel.com/new
3. Import your repo
4. Framework Preset: Other
5. Build Command: (leave empty)
6. Output Directory: (leave empty)
7. Add Environment Variables (see below)
8. Click Deploy

Option B — Via Vercel CLI:

```bash
npm i -g vercel
cd your-project-folder
vercel
vercel env add SUPABASE_URL
vercel env add SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
vercel --prod
```

4. Environment Variables

Add these in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables:

Key Value Environment
SUPABASE_URL https://xxx.supabase.co Production, Preview, Development
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY sb_publishable_... All
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY sb_secret_... All (server-only)
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME (from Cloudinary) All (Phase 5)
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY (from Cloudinary) All (Phase 5)
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET (from Cloudinary) All (Phase 5)
ADMIN_EMAIL wbullion0@gmail.com All (Phase 4)
ADMIN_PASSWORD (choose strong password) All (Phase 4)
EMAIL_USER wbullion0@gmail.com All (Phase 4)
EMAIL_PASS Gmail app password All (Phase 4)

⚠️ Never commit real keys to Git. Use .env.example for templates only.

---

🧪 Local Development

You need the Vercel CLI because the app uses serverless functions.

```bash
# Install once
npm i -g vercel

# First time only — links to your Vercel project
vercel link

# Pull env vars from Vercel
vercel env pull .env.local

# Run locally (serves /api and static together)
vercel dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000.

Plain python -m http.server or live-server will not work — the /api/env route won't resolve.

