---

🔒 Security Notes

· Publishable key is safe in browser code — protection comes from Supabase RLS policies (Phase 2).
· Secret key (SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY) is server-only. Never import it into any js/ file.
· Cloudinary API Secret is server-only. Client uploads use signed requests (Phase 5).
· All user data is served from Supabase, never hardcoded client-side.
· Vercel provides automatic HTTPS, DDoS protection, and the x-vercel-ip-country header we use for the Nigeria-only check.

---

🐛 Troubleshooting

Boot screen never finishes

· Open DevTools → Console. Check if /api/env returns 200.
· If running locally without vercel dev, /api/env will 404 → boot still completes but Supabase will be null.

Navbar visible on /reels

· The HIDE_ON array in js/navbar.js should include /reels, /games, /profile.

Blank page after boot

· Router didn't match a route. Check js/main.js — every path in the Routing Map must have a registerRoute(...) call.

"Supabase credentials missing" warning

· Env vars not set in Vercel, or you ran locally without vercel env pull.

Site not detecting Nigeria (or blocking Nigeria)

· x-vercel-ip-country only appears on Vercel-deployed URLs, not localhost. Local always allows through.

